      "problem": "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x\\to \\pi/8} \\left( 1 + 2\\sin \\left(2x\\right) \\right)^2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /8}{(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))}^{2} & ={(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(1+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(1+\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{2}+2 \\\\  & =3+2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
